There has been a lot of discussion recently about tough pets so I thought
I'd stick my oar in about it.
Started off as a Wizard (I normally prefer a Valk) with a wand of polymorph.
Obviously I zapped my dog. Lo and behold a pet Minator.
The Minator killed everything and I mean everything.
It killed 3 or 4 shopkeepers, wiped out the whole of the gnomish mines and
generally gave my weedy Wizard an easy time.
Trouble is, as I progress through the game I'm having a very hard time 
getting any exp points (the Minator also killed and ate my priestess) and 
worst of all my hard pet is eating everything it kills. I eventually died
of starvation in the bottom of the gnomish mines and now whenever I go down
there now it's not exeactly pleased to see me.

What's the chances of a scroll of taming working on the Wizard of Yendor
